  "term": "PNS",
  "definition": "PNS, or peripheral nerve stimulation, is a minimally invasive electroanalgesia procedure used to help relieve pain, especially neuropathic pain. It works by applying stimulation near a damaged nerve, typically closer to the body than the lesion site.",
